<Layout title="Resume | Andrew Smith" description="Resume of Andrew Smith, product designer and front-end developer." showFooterCta={true}>
<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>
<SiteHeader />
<main id="main-content" class="resume">
<section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Resume</p><h1>Developer, then designer, then leader.</h1><p class="hero-lede">Twenty years from hand-coded websites to product design in Agile squads. Currently studying product management. <a href="/work/Andrew_Smith_Resume.docx">Download the Word resume</a>.</p></section>
<div class="doc"><div class="doc-body">
<div class="role"><h3>Senior UX Design Lead &amp; Manager, Digital UX — RAA</h3><p class="meta">2019 – present</p><ul>
<li>Lead end-to-end UX and UI across RAA Travel (online search and book, and the travel agent booking system integrated with middleware), My Account, payments, renewals, claims and identity management.</li>
<li>Run discovery and delivery in parallel: member interviews, analytics review, design sprints and workshops.</li>
<li>Facilitated a design sprint that identified member identity matching, not payment options, as the real conversion blocker. It redirected the roadmap, and authenticated quote-to-buy is live for motor insurance.</li>
<li>Built research operations from scratch, introduced journey mapping and UX benchmarking, and contribute to design system governance, including a Vision Australia accessibility partnership.</li>
<li>Prototype working applications in code with AI tools, and manage the UX team.</li></ul></div>
<div class="role"><h3>Lead Web Designer, Senior UX Designer &amp; Front-End Developer — University of Adelaide</h3><p class="meta">2014 – 2019</p><ul>
<li>Designed and built the public website, student portals and digital products in HTML, CSS and JavaScript.</li>
<li>Custom-built a JavaScript design system adopted across all development teams.</li>
<li>Introduced UX as a formal practice, now a full UX department.</li></ul></div>
<div class="role"><h3>Earlier career</h3><ul>
<li>Web Designer and Coordinator, Viterra (2011 – 2013)</li><li>Digital Producer, Private Media (2010 – 2011)</li><li>Web Designer and Account Manager, Vmedia (2008 – 2010)</li><li>Freelance Web Designer and Developer, asmithdigital (2004 – present)</li><li>Hotel Duty Manager, Tower Hotel (1999 – 2008)</li></ul></div>
<div class="role"><h3>Study</h3><ul><li>Product Management, Udemy</li><li>Applied Project Management (Grad. Cert., in progress), University of Adelaide</li><li>Certificate in User Experience, Nielsen Norman Group</li><li>Human Centred Design, thishuman.com · User Experience and Usability, Userfocus</li><li>Multimedia Studies (Bachelor), University of South Australia</li></ul></div>
</div></div></main></Layout>
